WHY THIS FILE EXISTS
--------------------

The AGPL does not define or require a NOTICE file — that is an Apache-2.0
convention, and none of the 425 Apache-2.0 licensed crates in this dependency tree
ships one, so no obligation is inherited from them either.

It exists because Trynta bundles third-party assets whose licences require an
attribution to accompany the distribution: Creative Commons Attribution and
Attribution-ShareAlike marks, the SIL Open Font License, MPL-2.0 components, and
several per-brand permissions granted in writing. A single conventional file that a
packager or a downstream distributor will look for is the cheapest way to make sure
those attributions travel with the software rather than being left behind in a
source tree nobody redistributes.


